{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide"]}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"KeyValueStore","roleHeading":"API Collection"},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"title":"Reference"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a small protocol for one-shot scalar values that don’t fit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" model. Three implementations ship:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — production, backed by any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"type":"text","text":" suite"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — production, backed by the system Keychain (survives reinstall)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — tests, dictionary-backed, reference semantics"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inject through your "},{"code":"Environment","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", hydrate state at startup, and write from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effects. Reducers stay pure."}]},{"code":["public protocol KeyValueStore: Sendable {","    func value<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Value?","    func setValue<Value>(_ value: Value?, for key: KVKey<Value>)","    func removeValue<Value>(for key: KVKey<Value>)","    func contains<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Bool","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All values are JSON-encoded as "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Reads and writes go through "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which pairs a backing-store name with its "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value type at compile time."}]},{"anchor":"When-to-Use-What","level":2,"text":"When to Use What","type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Need"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Collection of identifiable entities (decks, cards, sessions)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Scalar preference (theme, sort order, last-seen version)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (UserDefaults)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Anonymous device identity that must survive reinstall"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (Keychain)","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is for many-of-a-kind data with change tracking and batched"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"writes. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is for one-of-a-kind values that you read once at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"startup and overwrite on change."}]},{"anchor":"UserDefaults-vs-Keychain","level":3,"text":"UserDefaults vs Keychain","type":"heading"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Survives reinstall?","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes (this-device-only by default)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Backup \/ device migration"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Included"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Excluded with default accessibility"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Throughput"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fast (in-memory cache)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Slower (system call)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Visible to other apps?"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No (per app\/group)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Optionally (App Groups via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessGroup:"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Best for","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Theme, sort order, feature toggles, last-seen version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Anonymous device ID, opaque tokens","type":"text"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Keychain costs more per access — hydrate once at launch and observe state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"afterward, never read inside a reducer."}]},{"anchor":"macOS-sandbox--entitlements","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"macOS sandbox & entitlements"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the data-protection keychain, so it never raises"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a user prompt — no “Always Allow \/ Deny” dialog, no locked-keychain prompt, no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Touch ID \/ Face ID challenge."}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"sandboxed"}]},{"type":"text","text":" macOS app still needs a keychain entitlement, even when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not sharing items across an access group. Xcode supplies an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application-identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically for provisioning-profile–signed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"builds; otherwise add an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keychain-access-groups"},{"type":"text","text":" entry:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["<key>keychain-access-groups<\/key>","<array>","    <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.example.myapp<\/string>","<\/array>"],"syntax":"xml"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without it, the first "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setValue"},{"type":"text","text":" fails with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"errSecMissingEntitlement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OSStatus"},{"type":"text","text":" −34018). This is a build\/signing condition, not a runtime"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prompt. iOS \/ iPadOS \/ tvOS \/ watchOS need no extra entitlement."}]}],"style":"tip","type":"aside","name":"Tip"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encryption, accessibility, iCloud-sync exclusion, and backup exclusion are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identical whichever entitlement you use — the access group only controls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which of your own apps"}]},{"type":"text","text":" can read an item, never third parties or the cloud."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a private device ID, in order of strictness:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most private:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" profile-signed build + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessGroup: nil"},{"type":"text","text":", relying on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application-identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" group. No other app — even same-team —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be entitled to it. Mirrors the iOS default; zero sharing surface."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Practically equivalent:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keychain-access-groups"},{"type":"text","text":" array whose only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entry is the team-prefixed bundle id (the snippet above). Use when a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"profile-signed build isn’t available (unsigned local \/ CI dev). Only delta:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a same-team app you sign could also declare that string."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intentional sharing only:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a shared group string. The "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first"}]},{"type":"text","text":" element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"becomes the default group for new items — never put a shared group first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for private data."}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Device-Identity-Pattern","level":2,"text":"Device-Identity Pattern","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The original motivation for "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" was apps without user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"auth that still want stable identity for analytics. Stash a UUID once, hydrate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":" at launch, feed it to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["extension KVKey where Value == String {","    static let deviceID = KVKey<String>(\"device-id\")","}","","\/\/ In Store.configured(), before constructing the store:","let kv = KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.myapp\")","let deviceID = kv.value(.deviceID) ?? {","    let new = UUID().uuidString","    kv.setValue(new, for: .deviceID)","    return new","}()","","let initialState = AppState(deviceID: deviceID, \/* … *\/)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then in the analytics plugin wiring:"}]},{"code":["AnalyticsPlugin(","    service: analytics,","    identity: AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.deviceID, properties: { _ in [:] }),","    \/\/ …",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure-based "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userID"},{"type":"text","text":" keypath runs on every dispatch, so the value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"must"}]},{"type":"text","text":" live in state — never call into the Keychain from the closure. Hydrate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once; observe state."}]},{"anchor":"Type-safe-Keys","level":2,"text":"Type-safe Keys","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare each key once on "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" so the value type travels with the name —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no magic strings at call sites:"}]},{"code":["extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == SortOrder {","    static let sortOrder = KVKey<SortOrder>(\"sortOrder\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == String {","    static let lastSeenVersion = KVKey<String>(\"lastSeenVersion\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then read and write through static-member literals. The compiler enforces"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that the value type matches what you declared:"}]},{"code":["let theme = store.value(.theme) ?? .system            \/\/ Theme?","store.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","store.setValue(.alphabetical, for: .sortOrder)","store.removeValue(for: .lastSeenVersion)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A typo or wrong type produces a compile error, not a silent miss at runtime."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Centralizing keys on "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" also gives you autocomplete and a single place"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to audit your preference surface."}]},{"anchor":"Wiring","level":2,"text":"Wiring","type":"heading"},{"anchor":"1-Add-to-your-environment","level":3,"text":"1. Add to your environment","type":"heading"},{"code":["struct AppEnvironment: Sendable {","    var keyValue: any KeyValueStore","","    static func live() -> AppEnvironment {","        AppEnvironment(keyValue: UserDefaultsKeyValueStore())","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"2-Hydrate-at-startup","level":3,"text":"2. Hydrate at startup","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read once into the initial state — never read mid-cycle from a reducer."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["extension AppState {","    static func hydrated(from store: any KeyValueStore) -> AppState {","        AppState(","            theme: store.value(.theme) ?? .system,","            sortOrder: store.value(.sortOrder) ?? .alphabetical,","            lastSeenVersion: store.value(.lastSeenVersion)","        )","    }","}","","let env = AppEnvironment.live()","let store = AppStore.configured(state: .hydrated(from: env.keyValue), environment: env)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"3-Write-from-an-effect","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"3. Write from an effect"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mutate state in the reducer, return an effect that writes the value:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["case .themeChanged(let theme):","    state.theme = theme","    return { @Sendable _ in","        environment.keyValue.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","    }"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try?"},{"text":", no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"do\/catch"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/setValue(_:for:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" does not throw —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder errors are programmer mistakes (e.g. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Float.nan"},{"text":"), so the store logs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them and triggers ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertionFailure"},{"text":" in DEBUG instead of forcing every effect","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to handle an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"text":" it can’t act on.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Testing","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Testing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Inject ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" and assert against the same instance:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@Test","@MainActor","func themeChangePersists() async throws {","    let prefs = InMemoryKeyValueStore()","    let env = AppEnvironment(keyValue: prefs)","    let store = AppStore.configured(state: AppState(), environment: env)","","    try await confirmation(expectedCount: 1) { confirm in","        store.send(.themeChanged(.dark))","","        for _ in 0..<50 {","            if prefs.value(.theme) == .dark {","                confirm()","                break","            }","            try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(10))","        }","    }","","    \/\/ Simulate a relaunch.","    let rehydrated = AppState.hydrated(from: prefs)","    #expect(rehydrated.theme == .dark)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tests touching real ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"text":" should use a fresh per-test suite and tear","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it down explicitly:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let suiteName = \"myapp.tests.\\(UUID().uuidString)\"","let defaults = UserDefaults(suiteName: suiteName)!","defer { defaults.removePersistentDomain(forName: suiteName) }","","let store = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore(suite: defaults)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Reads-Are-For-Hydration","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Reads Are For Hydration"},{"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" mid-cycle (inside a reducer) is an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anti-pattern. Reducers must be pure and synchronous; reads happen once at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":" construction. After hydration, the value lives in state and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"downstream code observes state, not the store."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" itself is thread-safe, but a reducer reading while an effect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes creates ordering ambiguity. Hydrate, observe state, write through"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"effects — that’s the discipline.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Failure-Modes","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Failure Modes"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Missing key","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/value(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Provide a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default at the call site."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Decode failure","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and logs through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os.Logger"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(subsystem "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"swidux\""},{"type":"text","text":", category "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"kvstore\""},{"text":"). On startup, behaves identically","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to first launch.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encode failure"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — logged at the same subsystem\/category, then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertionFailure"},{"type":"text","text":" fires in DEBUG so the bug surfaces during development."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Production builds log and continue; the in-memory state is unchanged. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API does not throw — there is no useful runtime recovery from inside an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"effect, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try?"},{"text":" would just hide the problem.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"anchor":"AppStorage-Interop","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"@AppStorage Interop"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"There is none, by design. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" writes JSON-encoded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"text":" blobs. SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@AppStorage"},{"type":"text","text":" only observes native primitive types"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bool"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URL"},{"type":"text","text":", raw "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"type":"text","text":"). Two parallel"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation channels — Swidux state and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@AppStorage"},{"text":" — would drift.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux state is the source of truth. Read once at hydration, then observe"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state through the store."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Schema-Migration","level":2,"text":"Schem